            <ArticleTitle>Structure-activity study and analgesic efficacy of amino acid derivatives as N-type calcium channel blockers.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2067-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The synthesis and structure-activity relationship (SAR) study of a novel series of N-type calcium channel blockers are described. L-Cysteine derivative 2a was found to be a potent and selective N-type calcium channel blocker with IC(50) 0.63 microM on IMR-32 assay. Compound 2a showed analgesic efficacy in the rat formalin-induced pain model by intrathecal and oral administration.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
